Is it possible to add a carry argument to the backward pass of a custom_vjp?  It would be useful for writing memory efficient gradients for invertible networks, in particular algorithm 1 of this paper https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/6c6d/753ff2093452323f1c20ac86f43e707fff6a.pdf.
I was imagining that the code would look something like this:
import jax
def low_mem_wrapper(flow):
    x_to_z, z_to_x = flow

    @jax.custom_vjp
    def low_mem_x_to_z(params, log_det_x, x):
        log_det_z, z = x_to_z(params, log_det_x, x)
        return log_det_z, z

    def fwd(params, log_det_x, x):
        return low_mem_x_to_z(params, log_det_x, x), ()

    def bwd(res, g, carry):
        params, log_det_z, z = carry
        log_det_x, x = z_to_x(params, log_det_z, z)
        _, vjp = jax.vjp(x_to_z, params, log_det_x, x)
        return vjp(g), (params, log_det_x, x)

    low_mem_x_to_z.defvjp(fwd, bwd)

    return low_mem_x_to_z, z_to_x

Thanks for the great work in JAX!

